.Dd July 11, 2026
.Dt GEMSTASH-METADATA 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm gemstash-metadata
.Nd extract gemspec metadata from the gemstash cache as NDJSON
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar gem-cache-dir
.Op Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
walks gemstash's on-disk gem cache, reads each Gem::Specification, and emits
NDJSON on stdout \(em one gem per line \(em for analytics with DuckDB,
sqlite-utils, or jq. Each record carries name, version, platform, licenses,
authors, homepage, summary, required_ruby_version, and runtime_dependencies
(name plus requirement).
.Pp
This exists because gemstash's Postgres database is only a thin index of what is
cached; the rich per-gem metadata lives in the cached .gem files, not the DB.
Stdlib only \(em no gems, no schema to maintain.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar gem-cache-dir
Directory to scan. Default: <gemstash base_path>/gem_cache, with base_path read
from ~/.gemstash/config.yml (else ~/.gemstash).
.It Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1
.It 0
NDJSON emitted; per-file parse errors are skipped and counted on stderr.
.It 1
The scan directory does not exist.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li gemstash-metadata | duckdb -c "SELECT ..."
Query the cache's license distribution or dependency edges.
.It Li gemstash-metadata ~/.gemstash/gem_cache > gems.ndjson
Dump every cached gemspec to a file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gemstash-ctl 8 ,
.Xr zsvc 8
